   "cast": [{"who": "me", "x": 820, "facing": -1, "pose": "shrug", "face": {"eyes": "flat", "mouth": "flat"}}], "speaker": "me"},
  {"set": "closeup", "state": {"show": "text", "big": "GAS|ATTACK", "bg1": "#FFE3E3", "bg2": "#D9534F"}, "text": "That gas floats straight up into your eyes. Your brain goes, nope, and floods them with tears to rinse it out.", "sfx": "busted", "meme": "shake"},
  {"set": "kitchen", "text": "And here's the wild part. For years, scientists blamed the wrong enzyme.", "sfx": "waitwhat",
   "cast": [{"who": "me", "x": 700, "facing": 1, "pose": "shocked", "face": {"eyes": "wide", "mouth": "o"}}], "cam": {"zoom": 1.4, "on": "me"}},
  {"set": "closeup", "state": {"show": "text", "big": "2002|JAPAN", "bg1": "#EAF3FF", "bg2": "#5A8FD0"}, "text": "In two thousand two, researchers in Japan found the onion has a separate enzyme whose whole job is making the tear gas.", "sfx": "ding"},
  {"set": "kitchen", "text": "A tear gas enzyme. In a vegetable. We put this on burgers.", "sfx": "bruh",
   "cast": [{"who": "me", "x": 700, "facing": 1, "pose": "facepalm", "face": {"eyes": "closed", "mouth": "frown"}}]},
  {"set": "kitchen", "text": "The good news? Cold onions sting less, because chilling slows those enzymes down.", "sfx": "sparkle",
